   "GUARD_WORKTREE_PATH_DRIFT": "WHAT: A task's worktree is not at <worktrees_base>/<branch>.\nWHY: Hammer owns worktree paths; a consumer resolving that task by name would read or write outside the registered worktree.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount <id>' to re-register, or 'hammer tasks doctor' for the full report. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Path resolution is ambiguous. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_MISSING_WORKTREE": "WHAT: A manifest worktree path is not a git worktree.\nWHY: The directory hammer registered is gone or was never created, so the task has no working directory.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount <id>' to recreate it. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: The task has nowhere to build. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_UNREGISTERED": "WHAT: A directory under .task-worktrees/ is not in the manifest.\nWHY: Nobody owns that path; anything resolving a task through it works outside hammer's control.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to remove unregistered directories, or move the work to the registered path.\nCONSEQUENCE: Phantom paths. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_WORKTREE_LOCAL_STORE": "WHAT: A registered task worktree contains its own .tasks directory.\nWHY: A worktree-local store is invisible to other tasks and can diverge from the central record.\nHOW: Inspect the reported directory, then remove or migrate it only after explicit confirmation.\nCONSEQUENCE: Divergent task records. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_ORPHAN": "WHAT: Worktree for task {task_id} has NO MATCHING BRANCH.\nWHY: ORPHANED WORKTREE. It points at a branch that no longer exists.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to reconcile worktrees. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Dangling workspace. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_MISSING": "WHAT: Task {task_id} has NO WORKTREE.\nWHY: {to_state} require a worktree for the task's branch.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount {task_id}' to create it. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Task cannot be worked on. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_UNAVAILABLE": "WHAT: Guard CANNOT VERIFY task {task_id}.\nWHY: Cache corrupt or git subprocess failed. Guard fail closed \u2014 a silent pass is the bug this tool exists to kill.\nHOW: Run 'hammer guard rebuild' then retry. --force overrides and logs the bypass.\nCONSEQUENCE: Unverified transition. REJECTED.",
@@ -68,5 +69,6 @@
